//! task: write
//! ask: Build a wire struct with a big-endian field and read the field back as a plain integer.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §5.2, §8.6
//! explain: A field declared `u16:maior` is a place whose bytes lie big-endian. Reading it yields an ordinary `u16`, and a literal assigns an ordinary `u16`: the conversion is the field access. A struct literal names every field exactly once, because missing fields are never zero-filled, which on a wire type would put bytes on the wire that no source line wrote.

@transitus
publica structura Cabecera {
    magia:  u16:maior
    genus:  u8
}

publica functio magia_de(c: Cabecera) -> u16 {
    redde c.magia;
}

publica functio facere() -> Cabecera {
    redde Cabecera { magia: 0xd3d3, genus: 1 };
}
